// HOLE 2 — no idiomatic subprocess surface: `std/process` does not exist.
//
// A subprocess-driven app (this whole region) must shell out to `git`. koru_std
// has fs / io / net / http / threading — but NO process/exec/subprocess/os
// module. So every consumer reinvents `std.process.Child.run` inside a raw-Zig
// `~proc <verb>|zig { ... }` FFI block (see koru-libs/docker/index.kz, and this
// app's own a_git_lines.kz / c_gitgazer.kz). That works, but it is raw-host Zig
// leaking into every app that runs a process — there is no koru-level, phantom-
// typed, effect-shaped subprocess primitive (the way std/fs:read-lines wraps a
// file read as `! line` / `| done` / `| failed`).
//
// EXPECTED: an importable `std/process` (or `std/exec`) with an effect-shaped
//   run/lines surface, phantom-typed like the rest of the stdlib.
// ACTUAL:   KORU002 module not found: 'std/process'.

~import std/process
